# A2/A2.1/A2_01_revision_and_word_order.letz
# Source: PDF slide deck "L1 a21lotsmanmeli.pdf" (A2.1 Conversatioun, Lektioun 1: eng Revisioun).
# Slide text was baked into the raster; transcribed from rendered pages, then every
# lemma verified against LOD (gender -> article; glosses cross-checked).
# The deck is explicitly a revision lesson, so words already taught in A1 are NOT
# repeated here as new Elements — only genuinely new vocabulary is listed, and the
# revision itself happens through the sentences.
# Grammar focus: inversion (an adverbial in first position moves the finite verb
# before its subject) — the harder half of A1's word order, drilled in both directions.

@lesson A2.01 "Revision & Word Order"

# --- Personal information ---
@word d'Mammesprooch = the mother tongue
@word de Zivilstand = the marital status
@word d'Aarbechtsplaz = the workplace
@word d'Hausdéier = the pet
@word d'Hausdéieren = the pets

# --- Free time ---
@word spadséieren = to go for a walk
@word de Tennisterrain = the tennis court
@word de Squash = squash

# --- Verbs ---
@word studéieren = to study
@word raschten = to rest

# --- Frequency & sequence ---
@word meeschtens = mostly
@word reegelméisseg = regularly

@sentence
@lu Wat ass deng Mammesprooch?
@en What is your mother tongue?
@distractor-en profession
@distractor-en where
@distractor-lu Beruff
@distractor-lu Wou

@sentence
@lu Meng Mammesprooch ass Ukrainesch.
@en My mother tongue is Ukrainian.
@distractor-en English
@distractor-en profession
@distractor-lu Englesch
@distractor-lu Beruff

